WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.537 --> 00:00:01.781
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:01.781 --> 00:00:02.638
I have to say too, God,

00:00:02.638 --> 00:00:05.301
you walked in today and I
just saw what you're wearing

00:00:05.301 --> 00:00:06.134
when we walked in and I was like,

00:00:06.134 --> 00:00:07.529
and then you walked out
today, like in this.

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:08.672
And I was like, oh my gosh.

00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:10.581
You, have you always been into fashion?

00:00:10.581 --> 00:00:11.414
- Yes.

00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:12.308
- Is it just natural for you?

00:00:12.308 --> 00:00:14.019
- Well, no, speaking
of the church, you know

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:16.343
the black church is a fashion child.

00:00:16.343 --> 00:00:17.176
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:17.176 --> 00:00:19.278
- And I'm first generation
post civil rights movement.

00:00:19.278 --> 00:00:21.238
So, you know, I was taught

00:00:21.238 --> 00:00:24.358
that the first impression
is what you look like.

00:00:24.358 --> 00:00:25.417
So, you must dress up.

00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:27.299
I came from the, you dress up in suits.

00:00:27.299 --> 00:00:29.729
I wore a suit to school.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.353
I wore a jacket and a tie
to public high school.

00:00:32.353 --> 00:00:33.186
- Yeah.

00:00:33.186 --> 00:00:34.019
- You know, dress for the job you want,

00:00:34.019 --> 00:00:37.002
not the one you have was what
my great Aunt Dorothy told me.

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:37.835
- Yeah.

00:00:37.835 --> 00:00:40.964
- So, you know, there were
lots of combinations of that.

00:00:40.964 --> 00:00:43.797
And then I've been able to now use

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:47.515
my fashion sense as activism.

00:00:47.515 --> 00:00:48.643
- Yeah. I like that.

00:00:48.643 --> 00:00:49.476
- [Billy] Yeah.

00:00:49.476 --> 00:00:50.309
- To make a political statement as well.

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:51.142
- [Billy] Yeah.

00:00:51.142 --> 00:00:51.975
- [Kelly] Yeah. And do you,

00:00:51.975 --> 00:00:53.174
I feel like every time I see you, like

00:00:53.174 --> 00:00:56.467
on a red carpet, like
literally you are a walking,

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.266
fashion but also slash
political statement.

00:00:58.266 --> 00:00:59.099
- Yes.

00:00:59.099 --> 00:01:00.405
- And there's always something
happening that that's deeper.

00:01:00.405 --> 00:01:01.347
And I love that.

00:01:01.347 --> 00:01:02.227
- Always dual, yeah.

00:01:02.227 --> 00:01:03.288
- [Kelly] Yeah. And that's on purpose?

00:01:03.288 --> 00:01:05.456
- It's always on purpose.
Everything I do is intentional.

00:01:05.456 --> 00:01:06.358
- Okay. I love it.

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:07.376
- Everything I do is on purpose.

00:01:07.376 --> 00:01:08.459
- Yeah.

00:01:08.459 --> 00:01:10.798
- You know, and, and because
I've lived long enough

00:01:10.798 --> 00:01:12.768
I've been in this business for 35 years

00:01:12.768 --> 00:01:16.406
I've made the decision that what I wanted

00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:18.454
to do as an artist,

00:01:18.454 --> 00:01:20.344
was to use my art to heal.

00:01:20.344 --> 00:01:21.302
- Oh yeah, of course.

00:01:21.302 --> 00:01:23.000
- My art, art is healing.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:23.861
- Because it's so healing for us.

00:01:23.861 --> 00:01:24.694
- It's healing

00:01:24.694 --> 00:01:25.527
- Yes, You wanna share that.

00:01:25.527 --> 00:01:27.168
- And I wanna share that. Yeah.

00:01:27.168 --> 00:01:29.496
- Yeah, I just saw those pictures.

00:01:29.496 --> 00:01:32.557
I wanna bring up the inspiration,
like your inspiration

00:01:32.557 --> 00:01:33.707
with the, with the fashion you've used.

00:01:33.707 --> 00:01:35.078
I wanna bring up those
pictures once again.

00:01:35.078 --> 00:01:36.928
This, I remember this first one,

00:01:36.928 --> 00:01:38.065
I think, were you at
the Oscars right there?

00:01:38.065 --> 00:01:38.898
- [Billy}] Yes.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:39.731
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:01:39.731 --> 00:01:41.993
- The Oscars, the Oscars was really where

00:01:41.993 --> 00:01:43.197
it's, where it popped off.

00:01:43.197 --> 00:01:45.087
There was a Golden Globe before that.

00:01:45.087 --> 00:01:47.654
Which was the first time
on a major red carpet.

00:01:47.654 --> 00:01:48.487
- Yeah.

00:01:48.487 --> 00:01:50.553
- But when the Oscars called, I knew,

00:01:50.553 --> 00:01:54.616
you know, this is the
entertainment Super Bowl.

00:01:54.616 --> 00:01:58.286
My friend Idina Menzel a few years prior

00:01:58.286 --> 00:02:00.976
you know, her name was
said wrong, and I saw

00:02:00.976 --> 00:02:02.347
- We, we all saw.

00:02:02.347 --> 00:02:03.180
- [Billy] Adele Davine.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.013
- Yeah.

00:02:04.013 --> 00:02:05.602
- And then she became a
household name because of that.

00:02:05.602 --> 00:02:08.234
And the businessman inside
of me was like, well, what,

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:10.802
when "ABC" called to ask me to
be on the red carpet, I said

00:02:10.802 --> 00:02:12.393
well, what is my,

00:02:12.393 --> 00:02:15.658
what is my wrong name calling gonna be?

00:02:15.658 --> 00:02:16.491
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:16.491 --> 00:02:17.324
- Like, what is it?

00:02:17.324 --> 00:02:18.439
- Yeah, what will be memorable,
but also have a message.

00:02:18.439 --> 00:02:19.272
Like I,

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.105
- Absolutely.

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:21.009
- when I saw that dress, I was like,

00:02:21.009 --> 00:02:22.580
well, hell, I'd wear that.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.222
Like, I, I love, I love that.

00:02:24.222 --> 00:02:25.055
- Yes!

00:02:25.055 --> 00:02:25.888
- Yeah!

00:02:25.888 --> 00:02:26.721
- And my thought was,

00:02:26.721 --> 00:02:29.068
you know because I used to
always say when I was in,

00:02:29.068 --> 00:02:30.658
at Carnegie Mellon Drama School,

00:02:30.658 --> 00:02:31.491
- Yeah.

00:02:31.491 --> 00:02:32.668
- We would have Oscar
parties and I would be like,

00:02:32.668 --> 00:02:34.487
I'm, I'm not gonna wear that penguin suit.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.096
I'm gonna wear, I'm gonna wear a gown.

00:02:36.096 --> 00:02:36.959
I'm gonna wear a gown.

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:39.468
And it's interesting
because words do have power.

00:02:39.468 --> 00:02:40.301
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:40.301 --> 00:02:42.517
- Even when you're not conscious of it.

00:02:42.517 --> 00:02:45.605
So 30 years later, 25
years later, whatever,

00:02:45.605 --> 00:02:47.277
I'm asked to do this thing and I was like,

00:02:47.277 --> 00:02:51.925
oh I remember I said I was
gonna wear a gown to the Oscars.

00:02:51.925 --> 00:02:53.576
And so I got to Christian Siriano

00:02:53.576 --> 00:02:54.666
and I thought, well, if it starts,

00:02:54.666 --> 00:02:55.999
- I love him.

00:02:55.999 --> 00:02:58.204
- if it's, if the shot starts here

00:02:58.204 --> 00:03:01.284
and it looks like just
a traditional tuxedo

00:03:01.284 --> 00:03:04.666
and then when you pull
out, it's a full gag.

00:03:04.666 --> 00:03:05.499
- [Kelly] I know because,

00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:06.332
- It'll change the world!

00:03:06.332 --> 00:03:08.385
- Because there's more than just the top.

00:03:08.385 --> 00:03:09.218
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:09.218 --> 00:03:10.051
- Yes!

00:03:10.051 --> 00:03:11.567
- There's more to, to a
person than even one outfit.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:12.400
I love it.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.767
I'm not, I am not that into fashion.

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:14.879
That's why I love watching it.

00:03:14.879 --> 00:03:16.567
'cause I'm, I don't innately go.

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:17.938
I am like the person you hate.

00:03:17.938 --> 00:03:20.527
I wear like workout clothes every day.

00:03:20.527 --> 00:03:21.778
And I don't work out on them.

00:03:21.778 --> 00:03:23.367
(Billy laughs)

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:25.508
It's like, look, they're comfortable.

00:03:25.508 --> 00:03:26.428
- Athleisure.

00:03:26.428 --> 00:03:29.258
- It seems practical.
I am 100% athleisure.

00:03:29.258 --> 00:03:30.679
- And you have two children.

00:03:30.679 --> 00:03:31.512
- I know.

00:03:31.512 --> 00:03:32.850
- And, and athleisure is cool now.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.708
- I would love to blame
it on the children.

00:03:34.708 --> 00:03:36.649
I was this on tour before.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:39.405
Yeah. I've always with this
person, but I love watching it.

00:03:39.405 --> 00:03:41.108
You know, I'm not a
painter, but I love art.

00:03:41.108 --> 00:03:42.290
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:43.679
- I love, I love all of that.

00:03:43.679 --> 00:03:46.388
But I, I have to ask too,
like, have you always had, like

00:03:46.388 --> 00:03:48.930
'cause I get so jealous
of such distinct voices.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.118
I feel like I have a good voice,

00:03:50.118 --> 00:03:51.238
- You have a distinct voice!

00:03:51.238 --> 00:03:52.668
- [Kelly] It's not
distinct. I'm a chameleon.

00:03:52.668 --> 00:03:53.501
- That's a lie.

00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:54.439
- No, no. I feel like my gift

00:03:54.439 --> 00:03:56.450
I feel like my gift is,
I can be a chameleon.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:57.283
I like going

00:03:57.283 --> 00:03:59.348
- You can be, and you
have your own distinction.

00:03:59.348 --> 00:04:02.272
- I don't know about that, but
I love, but like your voice

00:04:02.272 --> 00:04:04.936
like the certain level of
just like rasp and beauty

00:04:04.936 --> 00:04:08.220
to a voice that I'm like,
have you always had that?

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.063
Was it ever different? Or did you smoke?

00:04:10.063 --> 00:04:11.301
- Yeah. It was diff-, no, no, no.

00:04:11.301 --> 00:04:12.942
No, it was different earlier.

00:04:12.942 --> 00:04:13.775
- Okay.

00:04:13.775 --> 00:04:18.025
- My voice when I was young
was pristine and clear.

00:04:19.183 --> 00:04:20.016
- Oh, like a choir boy.

00:04:20.016 --> 00:04:23.530
- And really high, but like
Jennifer Hudson as a choir boy.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:24.391
- Yeah.

00:04:24.391 --> 00:04:26.927
- Like I was a high belting soprano,

00:04:26.927 --> 00:04:27.760
- Love.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.152
- like belt, belt, belt.

00:04:29.152 --> 00:04:29.985
- Yeah.

00:04:29.985 --> 00:04:32.814
- And then in 2001, right after 9/11

00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:34.784
I got severe acid reflux.

00:04:34.784 --> 00:04:35.662
- [Kelly] Ooh.

00:04:35.662 --> 00:04:38.495
- And my voice went away for about

00:04:39.454 --> 00:04:41.024
three or four years.

00:04:41.024 --> 00:04:41.857
- Oh!

00:04:41.857 --> 00:04:42.690
- Yeah, it was horrible.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:43.523
- Oh my God emotionally that,

00:04:43.523 --> 00:04:44.356
- It was one of the worst

00:04:44.356 --> 00:04:45.189
- I don't even know what I's do.

00:04:45.189 --> 00:04:46.022
- times of my life.

00:04:46.022 --> 00:04:48.900
It was the worst, one of
the worst times of my life.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.481
And my voice teacher Joan Lader

00:04:51.481 --> 00:04:54.001
and my doctors and everybody, you know

00:04:54.001 --> 00:04:57.020
really came together and took care of me.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:57.853
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:57.853 --> 00:04:59.658
- And a new voice emerged.

00:04:59.658 --> 00:05:00.491
- Yeah.

00:05:00.491 --> 00:05:01.969
- And I've leaned into it.

00:05:01.969 --> 00:05:02.802
- [Kelly] Oh, I love it.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.209
- And I love my new voice.

00:05:04.209 --> 00:05:05.042
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:05.042 --> 00:05:06.961
- And everybody else seems
to love the rasp too.

00:05:06.961 --> 00:05:08.620
- Yeah. Because them ears.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.409
(audience cheers)

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:12.700
- His new album is called Black Mona Lisa.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.189
I love the album title.

00:05:14.189 --> 00:05:15.022
- Yes!

00:05:15.022 --> 00:05:15.855
- Where did that come from?

00:05:15.855 --> 00:05:19.191
- Okay. So we were record-,
we were writing the album.

00:05:19.191 --> 00:05:20.188
I was doing a lot of writing

00:05:20.188 --> 00:05:21.260
with Justin Transer who you know,

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.093
- [Kelly] I love, love Justin, yeah.

00:05:22.093 --> 00:05:22.926
- who I love.

00:05:22.926 --> 00:05:26.207
And the team was all in there
and we're like six months in.

00:05:26.207 --> 00:05:30.827
And I don't remember
where the title came from

00:05:30.827 --> 00:05:32.840
but it just showed up.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.309
Black Mona Lisa

00:05:34.309 --> 00:05:36.152
and like the whole room froze.

00:05:36.152 --> 00:05:37.561
- [Kelly] And look at that art.

00:05:37.561 --> 00:05:38.401
Oh my God.

00:05:38.401 --> 00:05:39.733
- Yeah. The whole room froze.

00:05:39.733 --> 00:05:41.223
And I was like, oh my God.

00:05:41.223 --> 00:05:42.942
Oh my God. Oh my God.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:45.394
And then like 20 minutes
later, we had written the song.

00:05:45.394 --> 00:05:46.227
- Yeah.

00:05:46.227 --> 00:05:48.294
- And what I love about it
and what it means for me

00:05:48.294 --> 00:05:50.228
because this album is so personal

00:05:50.228 --> 00:05:51.668
and it's the first, it's my fifth album.

00:05:51.668 --> 00:05:54.089
And it's the first one where
I've written everything.

00:05:54.089 --> 00:05:54.922
- It's all original, right?

00:05:54.922 --> 00:05:55.755
- Except one song.

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:56.838
- All original,

00:05:56.838 --> 00:05:57.671
It's a pop album.

00:05:57.671 --> 00:05:58.743
I've written an all but one song

00:05:58.743 --> 00:06:03.242
and everything is from
the depths of my soul.

00:06:03.242 --> 00:06:04.496
I have lived a life

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:09.234
and I get to talk about that
life through the original gift.

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.067
- Yeah.

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:10.900
- Which is my voice.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.400
And so, you know conceptually,

00:06:15.842 --> 00:06:17.009
the Mona Lisa,

00:06:18.133 --> 00:06:20.300
is relevant, past, present

00:06:21.811 --> 00:06:22.644
- Will be

00:06:22.644 --> 00:06:23.634
- And forevermore.

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:24.624
- Yeah. It's classic.

00:06:24.624 --> 00:06:26.264
- [Billy] So I'm saying that about myself.

00:06:26.264 --> 00:06:27.097
- Yeah.

00:06:27.097 --> 00:06:28.224
- I'm claiming that about myself.

00:06:28.224 --> 00:06:29.914
You have to speak life into yourself

00:06:29.914 --> 00:06:31.216
- Yeah. You have to
know that about yourself

00:06:31.216 --> 00:06:32.896
and feel it about yourself if
somebody else is gonna see it.

00:06:32.896 --> 00:06:33.935
- [Billy] Correct.

00:06:33.935 --> 00:06:34.768
- Yeah.

00:06:34.768 --> 00:06:37.375
- So I'm, I'm learning to
speak life into myself.

00:06:37.375 --> 00:06:38.208
- which is important.

00:06:38.208 --> 00:06:42.958
- Right. Because if you, if
one can't sit in the fullness

00:06:43.874 --> 00:06:46.175
of their purpose, then we
don't know how to show up

00:06:46.175 --> 00:06:47.008
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:47.008 --> 00:06:47.841
- Properly.

00:06:47.841 --> 00:06:48.674
- Oh wow. I love it.

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:49.507
- You know what I mean?

00:06:49.507 --> 00:06:50.340
- Yes, I do. Yes.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.222
- And it's hard because,
you know, we live in a space

00:06:52.222 --> 00:06:56.280
where so many people have
opinions about stuff.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.400
And when you know who you are

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.262
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:59.262 --> 00:07:02.622
- And you can speak about that power.

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:04.502
Very often you're labeled as arrogant.

00:07:04.502 --> 00:07:05.335
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:05.335 --> 00:07:06.168
- Or narcissistic.

00:07:06.168 --> 00:07:07.001
- Yeah.

00:07:07.001 --> 00:07:08.480
- Right, and that's not the case.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:09.480
There's a difference.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.512
There's a fine line, but
there is a difference.

00:07:11.512 --> 00:07:14.430
And I have in, in the last few years

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.341
been able to find that power in my,

00:07:17.341 --> 00:07:20.924
in my life, in art, in
work, in everything.

00:07:22.363 --> 00:07:24.478
- I had an advice-

00:07:24.478 --> 00:07:25.344
Go ahead!

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:27.413
(audience cheers)

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:28.982
I had,

00:07:28.982 --> 00:07:31.995
somebody gave me advice a
while, years and years ago.

00:07:31.995 --> 00:07:32.953
And I loved it 'cause it was,

00:07:32.953 --> 00:07:34.195
it reminded me of something you said

00:07:34.195 --> 00:07:36.704
but it was like, take advice
only as advice, not gospel.

00:07:36.704 --> 00:07:37.537
- [Billy] Absolutely.

00:07:37.537 --> 00:07:38.584
- Because you know, you know your truth.

00:07:38.584 --> 00:07:40.851
But it's also great to hear
other people and their ideas.

00:07:40.851 --> 00:07:43.292
But at the same time, like,
especially with artists

00:07:43.292 --> 00:07:44.844
it's like, you know who
you are deep inside.

00:07:44.844 --> 00:07:47.245
Like, and what your purpose is
supposed to be as an artist.

00:07:47.245 --> 00:07:48.078
- Right.

00:07:48.078 --> 00:07:48.911
- Not to be like somebody else.

00:07:48.911 --> 00:07:49.744
So I, I love that as well.

00:07:49.744 --> 00:07:51.969
I have to talk about this
because I love these lyrics.

00:07:51.969 --> 00:07:54.763
Sometimes I fall into damaging thoughts.

00:07:54.763 --> 00:07:57.465
Right, that's a whole
conversation right there.

00:07:57.465 --> 00:07:59.765
Like, I don't deserve all the love I got,

00:07:59.765 --> 00:08:02.101
but then I take a second just to breathe,

00:08:02.101 --> 00:08:03.782
I always come back to me.

00:08:03.782 --> 00:08:05.735
What, explain what is that?

00:08:05.735 --> 00:08:07.272
It's very powerful.

00:08:07.272 --> 00:08:08.105
- As a,

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:11.472
black, queer man,

00:08:14.425 --> 00:08:15.592
in this world.

00:08:17.975 --> 00:08:20.255
I have been told for years

00:08:20.255 --> 00:08:24.172
and the messaging has
been that I don't matter.

00:08:26.433 --> 00:08:29.314
We are living in a time right now,

00:08:29.314 --> 00:08:32.274
where at the highest levels

00:08:32.274 --> 00:08:34.274
of government, churches,

00:08:35.916 --> 00:08:36.749
humanity,

00:08:38.304 --> 00:08:39.971
folks are dismissing

00:08:41.937 --> 00:08:43.607
entire groups of human beings.

00:08:43.607 --> 00:08:45.098
- It's like, we're going backwards.

00:08:45.098 --> 00:08:46.600
It's, yeah, we're going backwards again.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:49.808
- And the power has to come from inside.

00:08:49.808 --> 00:08:53.208
I, you know, being a gay man,
it's like the, the, the idea

00:08:53.208 --> 00:08:55.640
of like acceptance and tolerance.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:57.240
I don't need your acceptance.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:58.768
I don't need your tolerance.

00:08:58.768 --> 00:09:02.375
I demand your respect for my humanity.

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:05.837
Like I respect everybody else's.

00:09:05.837 --> 00:09:07.215
(audience cheers)

00:09:07.215 --> 00:09:09.353
- Amen. And then also when

00:09:09.353 --> 00:09:13.304
people start talking about
tolerance and acceptance

00:09:13.304 --> 00:09:16.389
that's so demeaning to me in
those words because I feel

00:09:16.389 --> 00:09:18.381
like, no, no, you should just love them.

00:09:18.381 --> 00:09:20.748
You, you can just love
them like who they are.

00:09:20.748 --> 00:09:22.301
- Well, it also puts the validation

00:09:22.301 --> 00:09:24.478
for yourself in somebody else's hands.

00:09:24.478 --> 00:09:25.331
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:25.331 --> 00:09:26.164
- Validate yourself.

00:09:26.164 --> 00:09:26.997
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:26.997 --> 00:09:28.942
- I don't need anybody
else to validate me.

00:09:28.942 --> 00:09:29.775
- Yes.

00:09:29.775 --> 00:09:31.752
- I am enough. Just as I am.

00:09:31.752 --> 00:09:32.585
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:32.585 --> 00:09:34.312
(audience claps)

00:09:34.312 --> 00:09:35.842
I guess I have two questions here.

00:09:35.842 --> 00:09:36.675
Like, how do you fight-,

00:09:36.675 --> 00:09:40.202
'cause they're, people are
being attacked like on a

00:09:40.202 --> 00:09:41.300
like you said, a government level.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.602
They're trying to pass laws that literally

00:09:43.602 --> 00:09:44.803
send us backwards.

00:09:44.803 --> 00:09:47.531
And that is fearful for
me as a mama as well.

00:09:47.531 --> 00:09:49.131
Not only for me in my everyday life

00:09:49.131 --> 00:09:51.574
but as a mom, raising
a boy, raising a girl.

00:09:51.574 --> 00:09:53.763
I want them to grow up in an environment.

00:09:53.763 --> 00:09:56.352
They can literally be
anything they want to be.

00:09:56.352 --> 00:09:57.441
And that is awesome.

00:09:57.441 --> 00:09:58.274
- Yeah

00:09:58.274 --> 00:09:59.107
- [Kelly] 'cause that is your purpose.

00:09:59.107 --> 00:10:00.065
- Yeah.

00:10:00.065 --> 00:10:01.371
- How do you, how do you keep the fight

00:10:01.371 --> 00:10:02.590
for that while also like

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:06.370
because the LGBTQ+ community
is definitely under attack.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:09.811
And so how do you, how do you
do that without, 'cause I feel

00:10:09.811 --> 00:10:11.310
like people are being like,
oh, they're being, you know

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:12.479
aggressive about it,

00:10:12.479 --> 00:10:14.910
or something and you're
fighting for what is just right.

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:15.743
- [Billy] Yeah.

00:10:15.743 --> 00:10:17.576
- Like how do you fight
for that in your way?

00:10:17.576 --> 00:10:19.326
- Well, first of all,

00:10:21.422 --> 00:10:26.172
respond, and don't allow
anybody to police your response.

00:10:27.379 --> 00:10:28.212
- Yeah.

00:10:28.212 --> 00:10:32.072
- There's a reason why I'm aggressive.

00:10:32.072 --> 00:10:35.272
You attack me, and then I'm the problem.

00:10:35.272 --> 00:10:36.214
That's called gas lighting.

00:10:36.214 --> 00:10:38.197
- Oh, I, I know it well.

00:10:38.197 --> 00:10:40.030
- So we're not doing that.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:41.714
So we're not doing that anymore.

00:10:41.714 --> 00:10:42.547
- Yeah, no, we're not.

00:10:42.547 --> 00:10:43.589
- But the thing that I move,

00:10:43.589 --> 00:10:47.554
the, the the thing that
grounds me is I'm 54 years old.

00:10:47.554 --> 00:10:49.285
I came out in 1985.

00:10:49.285 --> 00:10:52.710
I lived through the AIDS crisis.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:53.543
I know,

00:10:54.648 --> 00:10:55.806
that love always wins.

00:10:55.806 --> 00:10:57.248
I've seen it.

00:10:57.248 --> 00:10:58.613
It's a circle of life, right?

00:10:58.613 --> 00:10:59.676
(audience claps)

00:10:59.676 --> 00:11:01.277
- Yeah.

00:11:01.277 --> 00:11:03.517
- So what we have to do,

00:11:03.517 --> 00:11:06.574
